version: "3.0.0"
url: "https://github.com/creelie/geometric-selection-conjecture"
abstract: "Spectral calculations on the Dwork and weighted Fermat pencils, the mirror clause of the Geometric Selection Conjecture, one explicit tetraquadric datum audited against the nine conditions, and the proof that its two failures at the split locus are forced: every rank-five split bundle on a threefold with at most four Kahler parameters keeps an Abelian gauge boson massless, and the selection rules exclude six of eleven split data. The conjecture is not proved."
